.TH INSTALL 8 2026-10-25 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
install \- install an unpacked DarqOS distribution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /darq/dist/darq/bin/install
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B install
copies an unpacked DarqOS distribution from the staging directory,
.IR /darq/dist ,
into the installation root,
.IR /darq ,
and prepares the host to run it.
It is normally run by
.BR dui (8),
as root.
.PP
It performs these steps:
.IP 1. 4
Update the host's Debian packages
.RB ( "apt-get update" ,
.BR "apt-get dist-upgrade" ,
.BR "apt-get autoremove" ).
.IP 2.
Install the Debian packages DarqOS needs, including
.BR foot ,
.BR wayfire ,
Python 3.13 and PyQt5.
.IP 3.
Create the Python virtual environment
.IR /darq/env ,
if it doesn't exist, with access to system site packages.
.IP 4.
Install or upgrade the Python modules DarqOS depends on, then
reinstall the DarqOS runtime wheel from the distribution.
.IP 5.
Copy the p-kernel into
.IR /darq/kernel ,
and link its
.BR systemd (1)
units.
.IP 6.
Copy the DIDL tools,
.BR didlc (1)
and
.BR didlpygen (1),
into
.IR /darq/bin .
.IP 7.
Copy the manual pages into
.IR /darq/man ,
by section.
.PP
The host is expected to start from a Debian 13 (trixie) netinst
image.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /darq/dist/darq
The unpacked distribution.
.TP
.I /darq/dist/darq/lib/darq-0.1-py3-none-any.whl
The DarqOS Python runtime.
.TP
.I /darq/env
Python virtual environment.
.TP
.I /darq/kernel
Installed p-kernel
.RI ( pkernel ),
Python loader
.RI ( pyloader ),
launcher script
.RI ( darqos-pkernel ),
and its
.B systemd
units,
.I darqos-pkernel.service
and
.IR darqos.target .
.TP
.I /darq/bin
Installed DIDL tools.
.TP
.I /darq/man
Installed manual pages; read them with
.BR "man \-M /darq/man" .
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Progress is written to standard output as lines starting
.RB \(lq Ok: \(rq.
.SH BUGS
This is an early draft of the installer.
It does not stop a running system before updating it, configure the
host (locale, auto-login, the
.B darq
account), or restart DarqOS afterwards.
It doesn't distinguish a first install from an update.
.PP
Commands' failures are not checked.
.PP
It does not install services, types, lenses, or tools.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR didlc (1),
.BR didlpygen (1),
.BR dui (8),
.BR pkernel (8)
